<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haile Selassie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1975</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haile Selassie was the last Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, who died in 1975. He went into exile after the Italian invasion of 1935 and was restored in 1941 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>'s East African holdings collapsed. He pursued modernising reforms and became a prominent international figure, but was deposed in 1974, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haile-selassie.jpg" alt="Haile Selassie" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown; according to [1] and [2] an official portrait of which b/w copies were distributed by the Ethiopian government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haile_Selassie_in_full_dress_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
